  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Perimeter Solutions has $343M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date, distributed across 20 awards with an average award size of $17.1M. Obligations are up 7.5% year over year. Agency buying is concentrated: the Department of Agriculture obligated $227M and the Department of the Interior obligated $116M in the current fiscal year to date. Historical obligations show variability across recent years: FY21 recorded $164M, FY22 recorded $106M, FY23 recorded $89.9M, FY24 recorded $248M, and FY25 recorded $319M. The current-year totals are partial, representing fiscal year to date activity rather than a full-year total. The company’s award count and average award size indicate a mix of mid-size and larger awards. The three-year rise from FY23 to FY26 reflects higher contract activity, culminating in the FY2026 to date total of $343M.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are Perimeter Solutions’ biggest federal customers?",
        "body": "The Department of Agriculture is the largest buyer, with $227M in obligations in FY2026 to date. The Department of the Interior is the next largest, with $116M in obligations in FY2026 to date. These two agencies together account for the majority of the FY2026 to date obligations."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How has Perimeter Solutions’ federal business changed recently?",
        "body": "Obligations are up 7.5% year over year in FY2026 to date. Fiscal-year obligations rose from $89.9M in FY23 to $248M in FY24, then to $319M in FY25, and reached $343M in FY26 to date. The company recorded 20 awards in the current fiscal year to date, with an average award size of $17.1M."
      }
